From f7403c624a66e5638325972693f60220c6e73046 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suvojeet-sengupta <suvojitsengupta21@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:55:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: Add App lock to the apps settings

Android 17 has App Lock, but the only way in is the launcher's long
press menu, which Pixel Launcher doesn't have. Add an App lock page to
Settings > Apps that lists the apps App Lock supports, each with a
switch. Turning a switch either way asks for the fingerprint or screen
lock, then sets the app's App Lock state; opening a locked app, and
keeping its notifications and recents hidden, is the framework's own
App Lock. The entry only shows when the build turns App Lock on, and
the switches stay off until a screen lock is set.

Change-Id: Iefff525922778bbb04024b23fc8f34dfbc30cca9
